{
  "_about": "What each page loads, for the page-weight budget (budget.py; docs/performance.md). 'first': data files the page fetches before it is ready; 'later': data files it fetches on its own right after; 'on_use': data files it fetches after it is ready, the first time a visitor needs them (the map's index of the dictionary: the Catalog tab, the chat, the Economy tab; the dictionary's detail files: an entry opened, printed or exported), counted but not budgeted. The dictionary's Spanish (dictionary_list_es.json, 'later', and the Spanish detail file of each domain, 'on_use') is fetched by the Spanish page only. The area profile draws its first field, then fetches its 'later' files and draws every field. Every page but the dictionary also fetches the glossary highlighter's match forms ('later', once it is ready and idle) and, the first time a reader points at a word, its definitions ('on_use'; docs/glossary.md); the dictionary page reads both from its own copy of the glossary. Scripts and styles come from the page's HTML. 'budget' is in KB compressed: the map's is the plan's target (section E: 250 KB of data and 250 KB of scripts for the landing view); the others hold each page near its size of 2026-10-15 so growth is a decision. 'external' is the compressed size of each library from another host, measured 2026-10-15 (Brotli or gzip, as the host sends it; the MapLibre stylesheet 2026-10-23). 'deferred' lists the scripts and styles a page loads by itself after it is ready, not in its HTML: the base map of the 2D map and of the WCRP maps (js/core/basemap.js, MapLibre and its Leaflet bridge; docs/basemap.md), and deck.gl in the 3D view, which draws only its animated layers (docs/performance.md, 'Make room 4'); budget.py reports them apart from the first load, against 'deferred_kb'. tests/browser/throttle.js reports what a real browser fetches, to keep 'first' and 'later' true.",
